# Secrets. Every one of these holds a live credential — check `git status`
# before the first commit rather than trusting this file alone.
notebook/.env
notebook/credentials.json
notebook/token.json
notebook/APIKEyOpenWeatherMap.txt

# The backup notebook has the OpenWeather key typed into it, where the real
# notebook reads it from .env. Nothing needs the backup.
*.ipynb.bak
*.bak

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Accounts and wardrobes: real scrypt password hashes.
api/data/

# Dependencies and build output.
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.vercel/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Wardrobe photographs. These are somebody's actual clothes, so they stay on
# the machine they were taken on and out of the repository.
#
# `Images/items.json` is kept: it is the tagger's output and documents the tag
# schema. The seed loader skips any item whose photo is not on disk, so a fresh
# clone simply starts with an empty wardrobe and fills it through Add item.
notebook/Images/uploads/

# Working notes: the full setup guide, with absolute paths from the machine it
# was written on. README.md is the one meant for other people.
NOTES.md

# A Windows-only convenience wrapper around the two commands in the README.
start.ps1

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
.ipynb_checkpoints/
